## Traps carried forward

- A `dev → main` promotion DELETES the trunk (`delete_branch_on_merge` true + PR head IS `dev`):
  cut a `promote/<date>` branch for the promotion PR, never PR `dev` itself.
- A pre-commit AUTO-FORMATTER (Black/isort/whitespace) that modifies a staged file ABORTS the
  commit ("files were modified by this hook"); `git commit ... 2>&1 | tail -2` HIDES that line and
  a following no-op `git push` reads as "Everything up-to-date". Re-verify HEAD advanced + `git
  fetch` origin before claiming a push landed. (Hit and corrected this session.)
- `.git-`-prefixed scratch filenames trip the state-file guard — never name scratch `.git*`.
